WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.280
Security telemetry helps teams understand who accessed the system, which service acted, what policy decision occurred, and what sensitive resource was involved.

2
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:21.150
In AI platforms, that visibility may need to cover ordinary application access plus model gateways, retrieval systems, tool-use workflows, human approval steps, administrative changes, and service identities.

3
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:31.460
Useful defensive signals include authentication results, authorization decisions, denied actions, service identity use, administrative changes, secret access, policy evaluation outcomes, and unusual access patterns.

4
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:41.380
These signals help operators investigate whether a request followed the intended path and whether controls behaved consistently across clusters, environments, and data sources.

5
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:45.450
AI-specific workflows can make access questions subtle.

6
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:54.200
A user may be allowed to call an assistant but not allowed to retrieve every document the assistant can search.

7
00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:00.220
A service may be allowed to use one model route but not another.

8
00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:06.630
A tool invocation may require approval, a policy check, or a narrower runtime identity.

9
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.090
Telemetry should show the decision without exposing protected content.

10
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.140
Privacy-aware logging is essential.

11
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:21.720
Logs and audit records should avoid secrets, credentials, raw sensitive prompts, personal data, and protected source material.

12
00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:28.130
The goal is structured, searchable, time-aware evidence connected to request or workload context.

13
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.980
Security telemetry is not about collecting the most sensitive information.

14
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:39.390
It is about defensive visibility, accountable operations, and faster investigation with appropriate data minimization.

